.TH "CONTROL" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
control \- interactively control a radiod receiver channel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B control
.RI "[-v] [-V] [-s ssrc] [-r seconds] [radio]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
control discovers radiod instances or connects to the specified control/status
destination, selects a receiver channel, and displays its state in a curses
interface. It can change tuning, filters, demodulation parameters, gain, and
output settings. It controls the receiver; use monitor to listen to its
output. A matching command tag confirms receipt, not acceptance of every
requested setting. Unsupported or invalid settings may be ignored. Other
controllers can change the same channel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-s ssrc"
Select a channel SSRC. Without this option the program offers channel
selection.
.TP
.B "\-r seconds"
Set initial status refresh/poll interval in seconds. Default 0.25.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Increase verbosity.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH INTERACTION
Press h or ? for the installed keyboard help. Use Tab and navigation keys to
select fields; left/right select a digit and up/down change it. Frequently
used commands include f for frequency, m or p for preset, S for sample rate, e
for encoding, g for gain, and q to quit. Ctrl-L redraws the display.
.PP
Without a radio argument, the program browses _ka9q-ctl._udp services through
Avahi. Discovery requires the Avahi tools and appropriate network
reachability. Explicitly specifying the control destination avoids interactive
service selection.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
LANG selects the locale. A locale with digit grouping, such as en_US.UTF-8, is
recommended for the interactive frequency display.
.SH FILES
share/ka9q-radio/help.txt under the installation prefix contains keyboard
help. Preset choices come from the configured presets file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Discover an instance or select a particular channel directly:
.PP
.nf
control
control \-s 10000000 hf.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), tune(1), monitor(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
